## Control {{controlId}}: Limit System Access to Authorized Users

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization limits information system access to authorized users, processes acting on behalf of authorized users, and devices (including other information systems) within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant. Access is managed through Azure Active Directory identity governance and Conditional Access policy enforcement.

{{#if cuiGroupExists}}
The "{{groupDisplayName}}" security group ({{memberCount}} members) serves as the primary access control mechanism. All users requiring system access must be provisioned into this group by {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}. Membership is reviewed quarterly and reconciled against HR records to ensure only active, authorized personnel retain access.
{{else}}
A dedicated security group for authorized users has not been created. Access control relies on individual account provisioning pending group-based automation.
{{/if}}

{{#if policies}}
The following Conditional Access policies enforce access restrictions at the authentication layer:
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{state}}): Enforces {{#each grantControls.builtInControls}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}} for {{conditions.users}} users across {{conditions.applications}} applications.
{{/each}}
{{else}}
Conditional Access policies are not yet configured. System access is controlled through Azure AD group membership and application-level permissions only.
{{/if}}

{{#if infraResources}}
Supporting infrastructure:
{{#each infraResources}}
- {{resourceType}} "{{name}}"{{#if properties.retention_days}} (log retention: {{properties.retention_days}} days){{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Review Azure AD user provisioning records, security group membership exports, and Conditional Access policy audit logs.

